{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VRB7PanuCpkNssR6JdCXr8","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /ux/run/tmp/tmp.qY45iDC3W6/src/metais.yaml has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7159924f-09cd-4cbf-a94b-ddf0494030c4","uuid":"23650a34-ef93-4cb8-b922-71726f2fe34c","timestamp":"2026-10-21T14:28:58.297Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/ux/run/tmp/tmp.qY45iDC3W6/src/metais.yaml","oldString":"  its number and the date it was issued, the seller and the buyer, a table\n  of the items invoiced with each line's amount, the total, and optional\n  notes.","newString":"  its number, the date it was issued, the due date when one is given, the\n  seller and the buyer, a table of the items invoiced with each line's\n  amount, the total, and optional notes.","originalFile":"metais: \"1.0\"\nname: \"invoice\"\nversion: \"1.0.0\"\ntitle: \"Invoice\"\ndescription: \"Renders one HTML invoice, with a line for each item and their total, from a JSON object a program supplies.\"\nlicense: \"Apache-2.0\"\nguide: |-\n  This package renders invoice.html, an HTML page that prints one invoice:\n  its number and the date it was issued, the seller and the buyer, a table\n  of the items invoiced with each line's amount, the total, and optional\n  notes. The page carries class names and no style of its own.\n\n  It is written for a program, not a person. A billing job reads the\n  invoice from wherever it is kept, writes it as invoice.json in a data\n  directory, and runs two commands:\n\n      metais validate invoice --data data\n      metais render invoice --data data --out out\n\n  validate reports every value that does not fit the\n  [invoice schema](inputs/invoice.schema.json), and render writes\n  out/invoice.html. Every value is HTML-escaped, so a name, an address, a\n  description or a note may hold any text.\n\n  Each line's amount is its quantity times its unit price, and the total is\n  the sum of the amounts; the program supplies neither. Every amount is in\n  the invoice's one currency, given as its three-letter ISO 4217 code.\n  Leave notes out when there is nothing to add.\ninputs:\n  - name: invoice\n    title: \"Invoice\"\n    description: \"One invoice, as the billing program that issues it holds it.\"\n    schema: inputs/invoice.schema.json\n    forms:\n      - json\noutputs:\n  - id: invoice\n    template: invoice.html.liquid\n    escape: html\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":6,"oldLines":9,"newStart":6,"newLines":9,"lines":[" license: \"Apache-2.0\""," guide: |-","   This package renders invoice.html, an HTML page that prints one invoice:","-  its number and the date it was issued, the seller and the buyer, a table","-  of the items invoiced with each line's amount, the total, and optional","-  notes. The page carries class names and no style of its own.","+  its number, the date it was issued, the due date when one is given, the","+  seller and the buyer, a table of the items invoiced with each line's","+  amount, the total, and optional notes. The page carries class names and no style of its own."," ","   It is written for a program, not a person. A billing job reads the","   invoice from wherever it is kept, writes it as invoice.json in a data"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VRB7PanuCpkNssR6JdCXr8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
